# Apothecary & Chemist, Business District.
# Mr. Crane: dispenser of tinctures, camphor, and laudanum; observant of private domestic habits.
NPC: apothecary
LOCATION: business_district
SCHEDULE: morning=apothecary, midday=apothecary, evening=apothecary, night=closed

TOPIC: default
  GATE: NOT topic_done(apothecary, default) AND coat = plain
  TAG: apothecary_plain
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v1
  MR. CRANE: "Cough syrups and carbolic soaps on the lower shelf."
  [He washes a glass pestle in a pan of alcohol with methodical care.]
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v1
  MR. CRANE: "If you have a toothache, oil of cloves is ten cents a dram.\nIf it's nerves, chamomile tea is cheaper than tincture of valerian."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: NOT topic_done(apothecary, default)
  TAG: apothecary_badge
  VOICE: trombone_bureaucratic_medium_v1
  MR. CRANE: "Officer Corwin. I trust the precinct first-aid cabinet is adequately stocked with lint and bandages."
  WALTER CORWIN: "I'm not here for bandages, Mr. Crane."
  VOICE: trombone_pleading_medium_v1
  MR. CRANE: "Then please keep your voice down, Officer.\nPatrons in a chemist's shop are entitled to their privacy regarding remedies."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: visit_count(apothecary) >= 2 AND NOT (topic_done(apothecary, fenn_laudanum) AND topic_done(apothecary, the_stranger_remedies)) AND coat = plain
  TAG: apothecary_repeat_plain_sawdust
  WEIGHT: 3
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_short_v1
  MR. CRANE: "Mind the threshold, Walter. I've just laid fresh sawdust."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: visit_count(apothecary) >= 2 AND NOT (topic_done(apothecary, fenn_laudanum) AND topic_done(apothecary, the_stranger_remedies)) AND coat = plain
  TAG: apothecary_repeat_plain_mortar
  WEIGHT: 2
  [The chemist continues grinding sulfur in a shallow stone mortar without looking up.]
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v1
  MR. CRANE: "If you're looking for liniment, the shelf behind you hasn't moved."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: visit_count(apothecary) >= 2 AND NOT (topic_done(apothecary, fenn_laudanum) AND topic_done(apothecary, the_stranger_remedies)) AND coat != plain
  TAG: apothecary_repeat_badge_carboy
  WEIGHT: 3
  VOICE: trombone_bureaucratic_short_v2
  MR. CRANE: "State your business, Officer. Tincture of squill doesn't boil itself."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: visit_count(apothecary) >= 2 AND NOT (topic_done(apothecary, fenn_laudanum) AND topic_done(apothecary, the_stranger_remedies)) AND coat != plain
  TAG: apothecary_repeat_badge_curiosity
  WEIGHT: 2
  VOICE: trombone_pleading_short_v1
  MR. CRANE: "Don't lean against the counter glass with that belt, Officer. You'll craze the bevel."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: topic_done(apothecary, fenn_laudanum) AND topic_done(apothecary, the_stranger_remedies) AND coat = plain
  TAG: apothecary_exhausted_plain_prescriptions
  WEIGHT: 3
  VOICE: trombone_dismissive_short_v1
  MR. CRANE: "I have four prescriptions waiting for the evening carriage. You know your way out, Walter."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: topic_done(apothecary, fenn_laudanum) AND topic_done(apothecary, the_stranger_remedies) AND coat = plain
  TAG: apothecary_exhausted_plain_scales
  WEIGHT: 2
  [Mr. Crane measures grains of bismuth onto a brass scale, ignoring the bell over the door.]
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_short_v1
  MR. CRANE: "The drawer is locked and the ledger is put away. Good day to you."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: topic_done(apothecary, fenn_laudanum) AND topic_done(apothecary, the_stranger_remedies) AND coat != plain
  TAG: apothecary_exhausted_badge_odell
  WEIGHT: 3
  VOICE: trombone_dismissive_short_v2
  MR. CRANE: "Unless Captain Odell sent an order in writing, the counter is closed to you, Officer."

TOPIC: default
  GATE: topic_done(apothecary, fenn_laudanum) AND topic_done(apothecary, the_stranger_remedies) AND coat != plain
  TAG: apothecary_exhausted_badge_closed
  WEIGHT: 2
  VOICE: trombone_bureaucratic_short_v1
  MR. CRANE: "The precinct has its records, and I have mine. Neither belongs on display."

TOPIC: fenn_laudanum
  GATE: evidence(naomi)
  TAG: apothecary_fenn
  LABEL: "Inquire about prescriptions filled for Dr. Aldous Fenn"
  TIME: 5
  WALTER CORWIN: "Dr. Fenn was a physician, but did he purchase pharmaceuticals here?"
  VOICE: trombone_bureaucratic_medium_v1
  MR. CRANE: "A physician can prescribe, Officer. He cannot compound bulk spirits on his own parlor rug."
  WALTER CORWIN: "What did he purchase?"
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v1
  MR. CRANE: "Crude gum opium. And grain alcohol in four-gallon carboys.\nHe claimed he was compounding strong sedatives for severe arthritic agitation."
  WALTER CORWIN: "Four gallons of spirits is an excessive quantity for arthritis."
  VOICE: trombone_bureaucratic_long_v1
  MR. CRANE: "Dr. Fenn had forty years of immaculate clinical standing in Miskatonic County, Walter.\nA chemist does not interrogate a senior fellow of the Massachusetts Medical Society regarding quantities."
  [The chemist lowers his voice, adjusting a blue glass reagent bottle.]
  VOICE: trombone_haunting_long_v1
  MR. CRANE: "Though he ceased looking at his patients' eyes three months ago. Only their wrists and ankles.\nHe would press his thumb into the joint and ask them: 'Does the bone feel heavier to you when the tide comes in?'"
  NOTEBOOK: apothecary_fenn_supplies | "Apothecary: Fenn bought bulk opium and spirits; stopped looking patients in the eye, only examining wrists and ankles to ask if 'the bone feels heavier when the tide comes in.'"
  EVIDENCE: bulk_opium_spirits

TOPIC: the_stranger_remedies
  GATE: evidence(naomi) AND NOT topic_done(apothecary, the_stranger_remedies)
  TAG: apothecary_naomi
  LABEL: "Ask if Naomi Freeman sought medicine for her son"
  TIME: 5
  WALTER CORWIN: "Did the colored woman come to your counter?"
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v1
  MR. CRANE: "She did. The boy had angry red salt-hives along his shins from the weed on the low rocks."
  WALTER CORWIN: "What did she buy?"
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_medium_v2
  MR. CRANE: "Carbolic salve and zinc ointment.\nShe counted five copper pennies out of a handkerchief corner."
  WALTER CORWIN: "Did she speak of anything else?"
  VOICE: trombone_neutral_long_v2
  MR. CRANE: "She asked if sea water in this bay caused iron to pit faster than in Buzzards Bay.\nI told her salt is salt everywhere along the Atlantic.\nShe looked out the glass toward the point and said, 'Some water has more appetite than others, mister.'"
  NOTEBOOK: apothecary_naomi_salve | "Naomi bought carbolic salve for her son's salt-hives; observed that Widow's Bight seawater seemed to corrode iron unnaturally fast."
  EVIDENCE: water_corrosion_inquiry
